<title>UK: ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in November.</title>
<headline>ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in November.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The buffer stock manager of the International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) announced on Friday the buffer stock sales planned for November would total a maximum 4,250 tonnes and would comprise the following cocoa.</p>
<p>The date of the sale has yet to be announced.</p>
<p>Details of the cocoa offered for sale are as follows.</p>
<p> ORIGIN	   TONNES     PORT	 CROP	  QUALITY</p>
<p> Cote d'Ivoire     70	Amsterdam  1979/80     good fermented</p>
<p> Cote d'Ivoire  1,773	Amsterdam  1981/82     good fermented</p>
<p> Cote d'Ivoire  1,374	Amsterdam  1981/82     fair fermented</p>
<p> Cote d'Ivoire     99	Amsterdam  1982/83     good fermented</p>
<p> Cote d'Ivoire    556	Amsterdam  1982/83     fair fermented</p>
<p> Cote d'Ivoire    274	Amsterdam  1987/88     good fermented</p>
<p> Cote d'Ivoire     51	Rotterdam  1987/88     fair fermented</p>
<p> Togo		  54	Rotterdam  1987/88     good fermented</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom 44 171 542 8072</p>
</text>
